---
// Contour lines for the hero, exported from QGIS by the client 26 Sept 2026.
// Decorative only - it carries no information a visitor needs, so it is
// aria-hidden and the hero reads identically without it.
//
// Changed from the export, same adaptations the client's other artwork got:
//   - stroke:#0c538d became currentColor. The export is brand navy, which is
//     invisible against the navy hero; the hero sets a translucent white here.
//   - the repeated per-path style attribute (identical on every path but one)
//     moved onto the <svg> as presentation attributes. Only the long path
//     keeps its own, because it alone used round caps and joins.
//   - width/height in mm dropped; CSS sizes it.
//   - dropped: the RDF <metadata> block, the empty <defs>, the full-canvas
//     <rect> with fill-opacity 0, the 'Segoe UI' font attributes on artwork
//     with no text, and two zero-length paths QGIS emitted that draw nothing.
//   - viewBox tightened from the export's 0 0 3507 2479 to the ink itself.
//     The export left 31% of its width empty on the left and 19% on the
//     right, so at full width the contours would have sat small and adrift in
//     the middle of whatever box they were given.
//   - vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke". The supplied 3.07 unit stroke is in
//     viewBox units, and at hero size that scales down to about 0.76px, which
//     renders as a washed-out half-line. Non-scaling makes stroke-width mean
//     CSS pixels instead, so the lines stay crisp at any size.
interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props;

